(doc
  (title "YBS Framework Overview")
  (source-format markdown)
  (converted "2026-07-19")
  (section
    (heading "What YBS Does")
    (para "YBS (Yelich Build System) is a framework for building software systems with AI agents.")
    (para "**Core principle:** Specifications are the source of truth. Code is generated from specs.")
    (para "**Key features:**")
    (item "AI agents build complete systems autonomously from written specifications")
    (item "Zero interruptions after initial configuration")
    (item "Full traceability: every line of code references its specification")
    (item "Reproducible builds: same specs + same steps = identical output")
    (item "Language and platform agnostic"))
  (section
    (heading "How It Works")
    (subsection
      (heading "1. Write Specifications (WHAT to build)")
      (para "Create markdown files describing what the system should do:")
      (code "specs/
├── technical/           # Architecture, APIs, data models
├── functional/          # Features, user workflows
├── business/            # Requirements, success metrics
└── testing/             # Test plans, acceptance criteria"))
    (subsection
      (heading "2. Write Build Steps (HOW to build it)")
      (para "Create sequential build steps as markdown files:")
      (code "steps/
├── STEPS_ORDER.txt              # Execution order
├── ybs-step_000000000000.md     # Step 0: Configuration (always first)
├── ybs-step_<guid>.md           # Step 1: Project setup
├── ybs-step_<guid>.md           # Step 2: Core implementation
└── ...                          # More steps")
      (para "Each step contains:")
      (item "**Objectives** - What this step accomplishes")
      (item "**Instructions** - Detailed commands and actions")
      (item "**Verification** - How to verify the step succeeded"))
    (subsection
      (heading "3. Run Step 0 (Configuration)")
      (para "Step 0 asks questions and creates `BUILD_CONFIG.json`:")
      (code "{
  \"values\": {
    \"language\": \"Python\",
    \"enable_tests\": true,
    \"platform\": \"all\"
  }
}")
      (para "This config file enables fully autonomous execution of all remaining steps."))
    (subsection
      (heading "4. AI Agent Executes Steps 1-N")
      (para "For each step, the AI agent:")
      (item "1. Reads the step file")
      (item "2. Replaces configuration placeholders with values from BUILD_CONFIG.json")
      (item "3. Executes instructions")
      (item "4. Runs verification checks")
      (item "5. Proceeds automatically to next step (no prompts)")))
  (section
    (heading "Directory Structure")
    (code "system-name/
├── README.sxp                    # System overview
├── CLAUDE.md                    # AI agent instructions
├── specs/                       # Specifications (WHAT)
│   ├── technical/
│   ├── functional/
│   └── testing/
├── steps/                       # Build steps (HOW)
│   ├── STEPS_ORDER.txt
│   ├── ybs-step_000000000000.md
│   └── ybs-step_<guid>.md
└── builds/                      # Build workspaces
    └── build-name/
        ├── BUILD_CONFIG.json    # Configuration values
        ├── BUILD_STATUS.sxp      # Progress tracking
        ├── [source code]        # Generated code
        └── [tests]              # Generated tests"))
  (section
    (heading "How to Use YBS")
    (subsection
      (heading "As a Human")
      (item "1. **Write specifications** describing what you want built")
      (item "2. **Create build steps** describing how to build it")
      (item "3. **Point an AI agent** at the system directory")
      (item "4. **AI builds it autonomously** from your specs"))
    (subsection
      (heading "As an AI Agent")
      (item "1. **Check for SESSION.md** in build directory (crash recovery)")
      (item "2. **Execute Step 0** - Read BUILD_CONFIG.json or ask questions to create it")
      (item "3. **Execute Steps 1-N sequentially:**")
      (item "Read step file")
      (item "Replace {{CONFIG:key}} with values")
      (item "Execute instructions")
      (item "Run verification")
      (item "Proceed to next step")
      (item "4. **Update status** in BUILD_STATUS.sxp after each step")
      (item "5. **Mark complete** when all steps pass verification")))
  (section
    (heading "Key Concepts")
    (subsection
      (heading "Configuration-First Design")
      (para "Step 0 collects ALL decisions upfront. Steps 1-N run without asking questions.")
      (para "If BUILD_CONFIG.json exists, Step 0 skips all questions and loads existing config."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Verification-Driven Execution")
      (para "Every step has explicit verification criteria:")
      (item "Commands that must succeed")
      (item "Files that must exist")
      (item "Tests that must pass")
      (item "Expected output patterns")
      (para "AI agent verifies each step before proceeding."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Traceability")
      (para "Every source file references its specification:")
      (code "# Implements: calculator-spec.md § 2.1 (Core Operations)
def add(a, b):
    return a + b")
      (para "This enables:")
      (item "Understanding WHY code exists")
      (item "Updating code when specs change")
      (item "Regenerating code from specs"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Crash Recovery")
      (para "SESSION.md tracks progress. If interrupted, AI agent resumes from last checkpoint.")))
  (section
    (heading "Example: Calculator System")
    (para "**Specs:** Define a CLI calculator with add, subtract, multiply, divide operations")
    (para "**Steps:**")
    (item "Step 0: Collect configuration (language choice, enable tests)")
    (item "Step 1: Create project structure")
    (item "Step 2: Implement calculator module")
    (item "Step 3: Implement parser module")
    (item "Step 4: Implement CLI interface")
    (item "Step 5-7: Write tests")
    (item "Step 8: Write documentation")
    (item "Step 9: Final verification")
    (para "**Result:** Complete, tested, documented calculator in chosen language")
    (para "**Time:** ~3 hours of autonomous AI execution"))
  (section
    (heading "Core Value")
    (para "**Write specifications once. AI agents build complete systems autonomously, in any language, with full traceability and reproducibility.**")
    (para "YBS separates \"what to build\" (specs) from \"how to build it\" (steps) from \"the built artifact\" (code).")
    (para "This enables:")
    (item "AI agents to build autonomously")
    (item "Specs to remain current")
    (item "Systems to be rebuilt in different languages")
    (item "Code to be regenerated from specs at any time")))
